# KPMG Beyond: screenshots → TSX + YAML (do this every time)

Use this when building **pixel-faithful** KPMG Beyond components or **full-page** layouts from screenshots, and when adding **serialized Sitecore items** under `authoring/items/kpmg`. It merges UI discipline with **Sitecore CLI serialization** constraints so pushes do not fail.

---

## 0) Workflow — component by component (required)

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| One component per Cursor task (chrome → nav → hero → sections → cards) | “Build the whole homepage” in one prompt |
| `validate --fix` then `push -n production` after YAML changes | Push without validation |
| After YAML generation, run **`dotnet sitecore serialization validate --fix -i kpmgProject`** (or use `authoring/scripts/New-KpmgSitecoreFieldItems.ps1` / skills **sitecore-new-collection-yaml** / **sitecore-new-rendering-yaml**) | Hand-write field YAML under `Data/` and guess hash folders |
| Reference **KPMG / kpmgbeyond** paths in prompts and rules | Reference **Greeneking**, **Bupa**, or wrong vertical paths |
| Follow the **KPMG Beyond template folder structure** (§3.1) for every new component | Create flat templates like `KpmgBeyondXxx Template.yml` at `templatesProject/kpmg/` root |
| When creating a template, **always create its `__Standard Values` child and wire `__Standard values` on the parent in the same step** (§3.1) | Create `__Standard Values.yml` and forget the parent link — or add the link only after a CM pull |
| Use **exact Sitecore system template IDs** for `Data` sections and field items (§3.1.2) | Invent or typo system template GUIDs (causes push error: *Template ID … did not exist*) |
| Deliver **all layers in one task**: templates + rendering + placeholders + site Data + Home layout (§3.3) | Stop after templates/TSX — leaving out site Data or `__Final Renderings` wiring |
| Add rendering GUID to **Available Renderings/Beyond.yml** | Register TSX only in component map |
| Match existing **KpmgBeyond*** renderings for datasource wiring | Use GUID datasource templates or `@@name='KpmgBeyondXxxSections'` folder queries |

After each component push, verify insert options on a **Data** folder in CM, confirm the rendering resolves its datasource, confirm each new template’s **`__Standard values`** field points at its std-values child (§3.1.1), and confirm **sample datasource items** exist and **Home layout** references them (§3.3).

---

## 1) Clarify the design source (before coding)

- **Scope:** Single component vs whole page. A page may need **multiple components**, placeholders, and **separate mobile/desktop** treatments.
- **Breakpoints:** Note where layout changes (e.g. `xl` = 1280px for chrome offset). Match Tailwind to the design.
- **States:** Active nav, tabs, hover — list them; implement the critical path first.
- **Content:** Editable via Sitecore fields vs static markup — prefer fields + sensible defaults in TSX.
- **Brand tokens:** Use `kpmg-beyond-tokens.ts` and theme classes in `globals.css` rather than inventing new palettes.

---

## 2) React / TSX components (`industry-verticals/kpmg/src`)

### Structure

- Prefer **`'use client'`** when using hooks, `useState`, `useSitecore`, or browser-only APIs.
- Keep **`ComponentProps`** from `@/lib/component-props` and mirror **fields** to authoring templates.
- **Styling:** Tailwind in TSX; use `kpmg-beyond-*` theme tokens. Fixed chrome lives in `KpmgBeyondChrome`; main content uses `.kpmg-beyond-main-area` offsets from `Layout.tsx`.

### Pixel fidelity

- Reproduce **spacing, typography, border-radius, shadows** from the reference literally.
- **Images:** Respect aspect ratio / thumbnail vs hero rules from the design.

### Sitecore integration

- **`Placeholder`:** Dynamic names must match YAML placeholder settings — use `DynamicPlaceholderId` from params: `` `kpmg-beyond-main-${DynamicPlaceholderId ?? '1'}` ``.
- **Chrome layout:** `KpmgBeyondChrome` is fixed sidebar + header; `KpmgBeyondMainWrapper` only groups the main placeholder — do not duplicate layout offsets in both.

### Registration

- Add the component to **`industry-verticals/kpmg/.sitecore/component-map.ts`** with the exact **Sitecore Component Name** as the map key (e.g. `KpmgBeyondHeroBanner`).
- Set **`componentType: 'client'`** for client components.

