## 3) Serialized YAML (`authoring/items/kpmg/kpmg`)

### Paths and repo layout

- KPMG Beyond site content: **`/sitecore/content/kpmg/kpmgbeyond/...`**
- Module: **`authoring/items/kpmg/kpmgbeyond.module.json`**
- Project-specific items:
  - Templates: `authoring/items/kpmg/kpmg/templatesProject/kpmg/`
  - Renderings: `authoring/items/kpmg/kpmg/projectRenderings/kpmg/`
  - Placeholder settings: `authoring/items/kpmg/kpmg/projectPlaceholderSettings/kpmg/`
  - Site data: `authoring/items/kpmg/kpmg/site/kpmgbeyond/`

---

### 3.1) KPMG Beyond template folder structure (mandatory)

Every KPMG Beyond component **must** live under the **`KPMG Beyond`** template branch — **one component per branch folder**. Do **not** create flat items at `templatesProject/kpmg/` root (e.g. ~~`KpmgBeyondTopPicksSection Template.yml`~~).

**Canonical examples:** `Chrome`, `Communities Section`, `Hero Banner`, `Top Picks Section`, `Top Pick Tab`, `Upcoming Events Section`, `Top Pick Card`, `Event Card`, `Nav Link`, `Main Wrapper`, `Community Tile`.

#### Create templates in this order (every new component)

For each branch, create **all items below in one pass**. Do not push partial template sets.

1. **Branch root** — `KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}.yml` (Template: Branch).
2. **Datasource template** — `{Display Name}/{Short Name}.yml`
3. **`{Short Name}/__Standard Values.yml`** — create the child item first; note its **ID** (generate a stable GUID).
4. **Back-link on parent** — add **`__Standard values`** on `{Short Name}.yml` pointing to that ID (see §3.1.1).
5. **`{Short Name}/Data.yml`** and field items under `Data/` — **`Data.yml` must use the Template Section ID** (§3.1.2); each field uses the Template Field ID.
6. **Folder template** — `{Short Name} Folder.yml`
7. **`{Short Name} Folder/__Standard Values.yml`** — with **`__Masters`** (datasource + folder GUIDs); note its **ID**.
8. **Back-link on parent** — add **`__Standard values`** on `{Short Name} Folder.yml` pointing to that ID.
9. **Rendering parameters** — `{Short Name} Rendering Parameters.yml`
10. **`… Rendering Parameters/__Standard Values.yml`** — note its **ID**.
11. **Back-link on parent** — add **`__Standard values`** on the rendering-parameters template.

**Rule:** Every time you add a `__Standard Values.yml` file, **immediately** add the matching `__Standard values` field on its **parent template** in the same edit. Never leave this for CM or a later fix pass.

Reference: `KPMG Beyond/Event Card/Event Card Folder.yml` + `Event Card Folder/__Standard Values.yml`.

#### On disk (`authoring/items/kpmg/kpmg/templatesProject/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/`)

```
KPMG Beyond/
├── Chrome.yml                          ← branch root (Template: Branch)
├── …
├── Chrome/
│   ├── Chrome.yml                      ← datasource template (+ __Standard values → child below)
│   ├── Chrome Folder.yml               ← folder template (+ __Standard values → child below)
│   ├── Chrome Rendering Parameters.yml (+ __Standard values → child below)
│   ├── Chrome/
│   │   ├── Data.yml
│   │   ├── Data/{Field}.yml
│   │   └── __Standard Values.yml       ← child; parent Chrome.yml links here via __Standard values
│   ├── Chrome Folder/
│   │   └── __Standard Values.yml       ← child; parent Folder.yml links here + __Masters
│   └── Chrome Rendering Parameters/
│       └── __Standard Values.yml       ← child; parent Rendering Parameters.yml links here
```

Each **`__Standard Values.yml`** is a **child item** of its template. The **parent template YAML** must declare that link in **`SharedFields`** — this is not optional and not CM-only metadata.

Some `__Standard Values` items may serialize into **hash folders** at `templatesProject/` root after `validate --fix` (e.g. `CB6DE1B9F7015A66/__Standard Values.yml`). That is expected — the **Path** field in YAML must still point to the logical Sitecore path under `KPMG Beyond/…`. The **parent template YAML** (e.g. `Communities Section Folder.yml`) still holds the **`__Standard values`** link regardless of where the child file lands on disk.

#### 3.1.1) `__Standard values` on parent ↔ `__Standard Values` child (create together)

**Every** datasource template, folder template, and rendering-parameters template that has a std-values child **must** include this on the **parent** item:

```yaml
SharedFields:
- ID: "f7d48a55-2158-4f02-9356-756654404f73"
  Hint: __Standard values
  Value: "{STD-VALUES-ITEM-GUID}"
```

- **`Value`** = the **`ID`** from the child `__Standard Values.yml` (uppercase GUID in braces).
- Create the **child first** (or assign GUID upfront), then set **`__Standard values`** on the parent before moving on.

**Complete pair — Event Card Folder (copy this pattern):**

Parent `Event Card Folder.yml`:
```yaml
ID: "97acf665-1d92-48b4-a1fc-c87838718ab3"
Path: /sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/Event Card/Event Card Folder
SharedFields:
- ID: "12c33f3f-86c5-43a5-aeb4-5598cec45116"
  Hint: __Base template
  Value: "{A87A00B1-E6DB-45AB-8B54-636FEC3B5523}"
- ID: "f7d48a55-2158-4f02-9356-756654404f73"
  Hint: __Standard values
  Value: "{EF5EFF57-A2EF-4A2B-B11A-B67D363ACE1D}"
```

Child `Event Card Folder/__Standard Values.yml`:
```yaml
ID: "ef5eff57-a2ef-4a2b-b11a-b67d363ace1d"
Parent: "97acf665-1d92-48b4-a1fc-c87838718ab3"
Template: "97acf665-1d92-48b4-a1fc-c87838718ab3"
Path: /sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/Event Card/Event Card Folder/__Standard Values
SharedFields:
- ID: "1172f251-dad4-4efb-a329-0c63500e4f1e"
  Hint: __Masters
  Value: |
    {08185EEF-CACB-44B4-81CB-231122A7B3B5}
    {97ACF665-1D92-48B4-A1FC-C87838718AB3}
```

**On the child item:**
- Set **`Parent`** and **`Template`** to the parent template ID.
- For **folder** std values: add **`__Masters`** (datasource template GUID + folder template GUID).
- For **datasource** and **rendering-parameters** std values: usually no extra shared fields beyond metadata.
- **Never** add `__Standard values` on the std-values item itself.

**Applies to all three template types per branch:** `{Short Name}.yml`, `{Short Name} Folder.yml`, `{Short Name} Rendering Parameters.yml` — **three** parent↔child pairs when all three exist.

#### 3.1.2) System template IDs — `Data` section, fields, and branch items (mandatory)

When serializing template **structure items** (not datasource content), each item’s **`Template`** field must reference a **real Sitecore system template** that already exists in CM. **Never invent or “derive” GUIDs** — a single wrong character causes push failures such as:

`Template ID e269fbb5-a1d6-4586-b0ab-8792a3161594 did not exist`

Copy these IDs **verbatim** from existing KPMG Beyond YAML or from `authoring/scripts/Generate-KpmgBeyondYaml.ps1` (`$T_*` constants).

| Item you create | YAML path | **`Template` value** | Sitecore name | Notes |
|-----------------|-----------|----------------------|---------------|-------|
| Branch root | `KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}.yml` | `0437fee2-44c9-46a6-abe9-28858d9fee8c` | Branch | Parent = KPMG Beyond folder (`0b63eb74-c589-47c2-b3ba-9a10a3deb16f`) |
| Datasource template | `…/{Short Name}.yml` | `ab86861a-6030-46c5-b394-e8f99e8b87db` | Template | `$T_TEMPLATE` |
| Folder template | `…/{Short Name} Folder.yml` | `ab86861a-6030-46c5-b394-e8f99e8b87db` | Template | Same as datasource template |
| Rendering parameters template | `…/{Short Name} Rendering Parameters.yml` | `ab86861a-6030-46c5-b394-e8f99e8b87db` | Template | Same as datasource template |
| **Field section** | `…/{Short Name}/Data.yml` | **`e269fbb5-3750-427a-9149-7aa950b49301`** | **Template Section** | **`$T_SECTION` — required for every `Data` folder** |
| Field definition | `…/Data/{FieldName}.yml` | `455a3e98-a627-4b40-8035-e683a0331ac7` | Template field | `$T_FIELD` |
| JSON rendering item | `projectRenderings/kpmg/KpmgBeyond*.yml` | `04646a89-996f-4ee7-878a-ffdbf1f0ef0d` | Json Rendering | `$T_RENDERING` |
| Placeholder setting | `projectPlaceholderSettings/kpmg/*.yml` | `5c547d4e-7111-4995-95b0-6b561751bf2e` | Placeholder | `$T_PLACEHOLDER` |

**`Data.yml` — correct example** (same pattern as Top Picks Section, Event Card, Top Pick Tab):

```yaml
ID: "5a819213-2435-4031-d362-8192a3b4c5d6"
Parent: "9a3b4c5d-8e7f-4a6b-9c0d-2b3c4d5e6f7a"
Template: "e269fbb5-3750-427a-9149-7aa950b49301"
Path: /sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/Top Pick Tab/Top Pick Tab/Data
```

- **`Parent`** = the **datasource template** item ID (`{Short Name}.yml`), not the branch root.
- **`Template`** = **`e269fbb5-3750-427a-9149-7aa950b49301`** always — not another `e269fbb5-…` GUID.

**Field item — correct example:**

```yaml
ID: "6b829324-3546-4142-e473-92a3b4c5d6e7"
Parent: "5a819213-2435-4031-d362-8192a3b4c5d6"
Template: "455a3e98-a627-4b40-8035-e683a0331ac7"
Path: /sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/Top Pick Tab/Top Pick Tab/Data/TabLabel
SharedFields:
- ID: "ab162cc0-dc80-4abf-8871-998ee5d7ba32"
  Hint: Type
  Value: "Single-Line Text"
```

**Std-values child items** are different: their **`Template`** is the **parent template’s ID** (the datasource/folder/rendering-params template you just created), **not** a system template ID. See §3.1.1.

**Before push:** grep new YAML for `Template:` and confirm every `Data.yml` line matches `e269fbb5-3750-427a-9149-7aa950b49301`. Reference siblings: `KPMG Beyond/Top Picks Section/Top Picks Section/Data.yml`, `KPMG Beyond/Event Card/Event Card/Data.yml`.

#### In Sitecore (Path field in each YAML)

| Item | Path pattern |
|------|----------------|
| Branch root | `/sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}` |
| Datasource template | `/sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}/{Short Name}` |
| Folder template | `/sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}/{Short Name} Folder` |
| Rendering parameters | `/sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}/{Short Name} Rendering Parameters` |
| Field section | `…/{Short Name}/Data` |
| Field | `…/{Short Name}/Data/{FieldName}` |

- **Branch root** parent: `KPMG Beyond` folder (`0b63eb74-c589-47c2-b3ba-9a10a3deb16f`), template **`0437fee2-44c9-46a6-abe9-28858d9fee8c`** (Branch).
- **All child templates** parent: the branch root item ID — **not** the generic `kpmg` project folder.
- **Short Name** matches the human-readable component name (`Chrome`, `Top Picks Section`, `Community Tile`, …) — not the React/export prefix `KpmgBeyond`.

#### Folder template — insert options (`__Masters` on std-values child)

Every **`{Short Name} Folder/__Standard Values`** item **must** define **`__Masters`** (in addition to being linked from the parent folder template via **`__Standard values`**):

```yaml
SharedFields:
- ID: "1172f251-dad4-4efb-a329-0c63500e4f1e"
  Hint: __Masters
  Value: |
    {DATASOURCE-TEMPLATE-GUID}
    {FOLDER-TEMPLATE-GUID}
```

- First GUID: the **datasource template** (e.g. `{Short Name}`).
- Second GUID: the **folder template** itself (allows nested folders).
- Reference: `KPMG Beyond/Chrome/Chrome Folder/__Standard Values.yml`, `Communities Section/Communities Section Folder/__Standard Values.yml`.

Card-level folders (Top Pick Card, Event Card, Community Tile, Nav Link) follow the same pattern under their own branch.

#### Naming anti-patterns (never do this)

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| `KpmgBeyondTopPicksSection Template.yml` at `kpmg/` root | `KPMG Beyond/Top Picks Section/Top Picks Section.yml` |
| Path `/sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KpmgBeyondTopPicksSection Template` | Path `/sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/Top Picks Section/Top Picks Section` |
| Parent = generic kpmg project folder | Parent = branch root under `KPMG Beyond` |
| Folder std values without `__Masters` | `__Masters` with datasource + folder template IDs |
| Template with `__Standard Values` child but no `__Standard values` on parent | Parent `SharedFields` links to std-values item GUID |
| **`Data.yml` with wrong `Template` GUID** (e.g. `e269fbb5-a1d6-…`) | **`Template: "e269fbb5-3750-427a-9149-7aa950b49301"`** on every field section (§3.1.2) |
| Field item with invented template ID | **`Template: "455a3e98-a627-4b40-8035-e683a0331ac7"`** on every `Data/{Field}.yml` |

