### 3.2) Rendering items (JSON rendering)

Reference implementations: `KpmgBeyondChrome.yml`, `KpmgBeyondCommunitiesSection.yml`, `KpmgBeyondHeroBanner.yml`, `KpmgBeyondTopPicksSection.yml`, `KpmgBeyondTopPickTab.yml`.

- **File name:** `KpmgBeyond{Component}.yml` under `projectRenderings/kpmg/`.
- **`componentName`:** must match **`component-map.ts`** (e.g. `KpmgBeyondChrome`).
- **`Placeholders`:** shared field with placeholder-setting item IDs when the component exposes placeholders.

#### Datasource Template — use path strings, not GUIDs

```yaml
- ID: "1a7c85e5-dc0b-490d-9187-bb1dbcb4c72f"
  Hint: Datasource Template
  Value: /sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/Chrome/Chrome
```

#### Datasource Location — query by folder **template name**, not content folder item name

```yaml
- ID: "b5b27af1-25ef-405c-87ce-369b3a004016"
  Hint: Datasource Location
  Value: "query:$site/*[@@name='Data']/*[@@templatename='Chrome Folder']|query:$sharedSites/*[@@name='Data']/*[@@templatename='Chrome Folder']"
```

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| `Value: {01739FEC-A4AC-4617-B218-DB735ED68002}` | `Value: /sitecore/templates/Project/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/Top Picks Section/Top Picks Section` |
| `*[@@[@@name='KpmgBeyondTopPicksSections']` | `*[@@[@@templatename='Top Picks Section Folder']` |

- **`Parameters Template`:** GUID of `{Short Name} Rendering Parameters` is fine.
- Site **Data** folders may keep legacy folder **item names** (e.g. `KpmgBeyondTopPicksSections`); the rendering query targets the **folder template**, so names need not match.

### Placeholder settings

- Create under `projectPlaceholderSettings/kpmg/`.
- **Placeholder Key:** use `{*}` for dynamic segments (e.g. `kpmg-beyond-main-{*}`).
- **Allowed Controls:** reference rendering IDs allowed in that placeholder.

### Available renderings

- Append new rendering item **IDs** to **`Presentation/Available Renderings/Beyond.yml`**.

### Site Data folders and sample content (§3.3)

- Data folder items under `site/kpmgbeyond/Data/` use the **`{Short Name} Folder`** template (by GUID).
- Verify folder template GUID matches the YAML under `KPMG Beyond/{Component}/{Short Name} Folder.yml`.
- **Always** add at least one sample datasource item under the Data folder in the same task.

### 3.3) Full component delivery — templates + project items + site data + layout (mandatory)

When adding **any** new KPMG Beyond component, deliver **all layers below in the same task**. Do not consider the component done until every row is checked. Stopping after templates + TSX (without site Data and page layout) is the most common cause of “rendering exists but nothing shows on the page”.

#### Delivery checklist (every new component)

| # | Layer | On-disk location | Required when |
|---|--------|------------------|---------------|
| 1 | **Template branch** | `templatesProject/kpmg/KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}/` | Always (§3.1) |
| 2 | **JSON rendering** | `projectRenderings/kpmg/KpmgBeyond{ExportName}.yml` | Always (§3.2) |
| 3 | **Placeholder settings** | `projectPlaceholderSettings/kpmg/kpmg-beyond-*.yml` | Component uses `<Placeholder>` in TSX |
| 4 | **Available renderings** | `site/kpmgbeyond/Presentation/Available Renderings/Beyond.yml` | Always — append rendering item GUID |
| 5 | **TSX + component map** | `src/components/kpmg/` + `.sitecore/component-map.ts` | Always (§2) |
| 6 | **Site Data folder** | `site/kpmgbeyond/Data/KpmgBeyond{DataFolder}.yml` | Datasource-backed components |
| 7 | **Sample datasource item(s)** | `site/kpmgbeyond/Data/KpmgBeyond{DataFolder}/{Sample}.yml` | Always ≥1 sample per datasource type |
| 8 | **Home page layout** | `site/kpmgbeyond/Home.yml` → `__Final Renderings` | Component appears on Home (or target page) |

**Rule:** If the component has **child placeholders** (section → tab → card), also create site Data + sample items + layout wiring for **each child component type** — not just the parent section.

#### Site Data folder (step 6)

Content folder under `/sitecore/content/kpmg/kpmgbeyond/Data/`. Naming follows existing convention: **`KpmgBeyond` + plural export name** (e.g. `KpmgBeyondTopPickTabs`, `KpmgBeyondEventCards`, `KpmgBeyondTopPicksSections`).

```yaml
ID: "{STABLE-GUID}"
Parent: "5ffbaddc-e2df-4ddf-b264-4fd8c60a42c7"
Template: "{SHORT-NAME-FOLDER-TEMPLATE-GUID}"
Path: /sitecore/content/kpmg/kpmgbeyond/Data/KpmgBeyondTopPickTabs
```

- **`Template`** = the **`{Short Name} Folder`** template GUID from `KPMG Beyond/{Display Name}/{Short Name} Folder.yml` — **not** a generic Sitecore folder template.
- **`Parent`** = site Data root (`5ffbaddc-e2df-4ddf-b264-4fd8c60a42c7`).

Reference: `Data/KpmgBeyondTopPickCards.yml` (template `92b4ebea-…` = Top Pick Card Folder), `Data/KpmgBeyondTopPickTabs.yml` (template `0b4c5d6e-…` = Top Pick Tab Folder).

#### Sample datasource items (step 7)

Create at least one YAML item per datasource template so authors (and Home layout) have content to bind:

```yaml
ID: "{STABLE-GUID}"
Parent: "{DATA-FOLDER-GUID}"
Template: "{DATASOURCE-TEMPLATE-GUID}"
Path: /sitecore/content/kpmg/kpmgbeyond/Data/KpmgBeyondTopPickTabs/Recommended
Languages:
- Language: en
  Versions:
  - Version: 1
    Fields:
    - ID: "{FIELD-GUID}"
      Hint: TabLabel
      Value: Recommended
    # … all meaningful fields populated with realistic defaults
```

- **`Template`** = datasource template GUID (`{Short Name}.yml` under the branch).
- Populate **every field** the TSX reads (plus Link/Image with valid serialized values).
- For **card/tile** components: add multiple sample items when useful (see `KpmgBeyondTopPickCards/`, `KpmgBeyondEventCards/`).

Reference: `Data/KpmgBeyondTopPickTabs/Recommended.yml`, `Data/KpmgBeyondTopPickTabs/Discover.yml`, `Data/KpmgBeyondTopPicksSections/Home Top Picks.yml`.

#### Home page layout — `__Final Renderings` (step 8)

Wire the component on **`site/kpmgbeyond/Home.yml`** (or the target page) in the **`__Final Renderings`** field. Match placeholder keys and `DynamicPlaceholderId` values to TSX.

**Section on main placeholder:**

```xml
<r
  uid="{UNIQUE-UID}"
  s:ds="{SECTION-DATASOURCE-GUID}"
  s:id="{SECTION-RENDERING-GUID}"
  s:par="…&amp;DynamicPlaceholderId=4"
  s:ph="headless-main" />
```

**Child in section placeholder** (placeholder key from TSX: `` `kpmg-beyond-top-pick-tabs-${DynamicPlaceholderId}` `` → `kpmg-beyond-top-pick-tabs-4`):

```xml
<r
  uid="{UNIQUE-UID}"
  s:ds="{TAB-DATASOURCE-GUID}"
  s:id="{TAB-RENDERING-GUID}"
  s:par="…&amp;DynamicPlaceholderId=1"
  s:ph="/headless-main/kpmg-beyond-top-pick-tabs-4" />
```

**Grandchild in nested placeholder** (tab cards: `` `kpmg-beyond-top-pick-cards-${DynamicPlaceholderId}` ``):

```xml
<r
  uid="{UNIQUE-UID}"
  s:ds="{CARD-DATASOURCE-GUID}"
  s:id="{CARD-RENDERING-GUID}"
  s:par="…&amp;DynamicPlaceholderId=1"
  s:ph="/headless-main/kpmg-beyond-top-pick-tabs-4/kpmg-beyond-top-pick-cards-1" />
```

- **`s:ds`** = site **content item** GUID (sample datasource), not the rendering GUID.
- **`s:id`** = JSON **rendering** item GUID from `projectRenderings/kpmg/`.
- **`s:ph`** = full placeholder path: `/headless-main/{parent-ph}/{child-ph}` for nested placeholders.
- **`DynamicPlaceholderId`** on parent and children must match the suffix in each placeholder key (`-4`, `-1`, `-2`, …).
- Maintain **`p:after`** ordering so the rendering chain is valid XML.

**Reference layout — Top Picks (section → tabs → cards):**

```
Home __Final Renderings
└─ KpmgBeyondTopPicksSection (ds: Home Top Picks, DynamicPlaceholderId=4)
     └─ kpmg-beyond-top-pick-tabs-4
          ├─ KpmgBeyondTopPickTab Recommended (DynamicPlaceholderId=1)
          │    └─ kpmg-beyond-top-pick-cards-1 → KpmgBeyondTopPickCard × n
          └─ KpmgBeyondTopPickTab Discover (DynamicPlaceholderId=2)
               └─ kpmg-beyond-top-pick-cards-2 → KpmgBeyondTopPickCard × n
```

**Simpler pattern — Communities (section → tile):**

```
KpmgBeyondCommunitiesSection (DynamicPlaceholderId=1)
└─ kpmg-beyond-communities-1 → KpmgBeyondCommunityTile
```

**Simpler pattern — Events (section → cards):**

```
KpmgBeyondUpcomingEventsSection (DynamicPlaceholderId=5)
└─ kpmg-beyond-events-5 → KpmgBeyondEventCard × n
```

#### Nested / multi-component tasks

When a feature spans **multiple components** (e.g. Top Pick Tab inside Top Picks Section):

1. Create template branches for **each** component type.
2. Create renderings + placeholder settings for **each** placeholder key.
3. Create **separate** site Data folders: `KpmgBeyondTopPicksSections`, `KpmgBeyondTopPickTabs`, `KpmgBeyondTopPickCards`.
4. Add sample items to **each** folder.
5. Wire **full hierarchy** in `Home.yml` — parent section, then tabs, then cards.

#### Anti-patterns (§3.3)

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| Templates + `KpmgBeyondXxx.yml` rendering only | Also `Data/KpmgBeyondXxxs.yml` + sample datasource + Home layout |
| Site Data folder with generic folder template (`35bf2b90-…`) | **`{Short Name} Folder`** template GUID from the branch |
| Rendering on page with no `s:ds` sample item | Create datasource YAML; reference its GUID in layout |
| Tab/card renderings missing from `__Final Renderings` | Add all levels: section → child → grandchild |
| Placeholder path `kpmg-beyond-top-pick-cards-1` without parent prefix | `/headless-main/kpmg-beyond-top-pick-tabs-4/kpmg-beyond-top-pick-cards-1` |
| GUIDs in rendering YAML with spaces `{ GUID }` | `{GUID}` — no spaces inside braces |

